1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,744
Welcome to the last lesson of Module 6.

2
00:00:02,744 --> 00:00:06,945
Now that your deals are on the board,
let's read the numbers behind them.

3
00:00:06,945 --> 00:00:09,649
You'll learn where to
see your conversion rate,

4
00:00:09,649 --> 00:00:13,619
how to spot the stage where deals
get stuck, and what to do about it.

5
00:00:14,493 --> 00:00:17,213
Your pipeline reports
live on the dashboard.

6
00:00:17,213 --> 00:00:20,119
Every opportunity widget
has a pipeline filter,

7
00:00:20,119 --> 00:00:23,520
so check that it's showing
the pipeline you care about.

8
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:25,807
Here, they're all on Patient Journey.

9
00:00:26,658 --> 00:00:29,814
Opportunity status tells
you how many deals you have,

10
00:00:29,814 --> 00:00:32,850
and opportunity value tells
you what they're worth.

11
00:00:32,850 --> 00:00:34,756
Watch the open number over time.

12
00:00:34,756 --> 00:00:39,043
If it shrinks week after week, you
need more leads coming in at the top.

13
00:00:39,893 --> 00:00:43,457
Conversion rate is the
share of deals you've won.

14
00:00:43,457 --> 00:00:45,494
In Patient Journey it's 25%.

15
00:00:45,494 --> 00:00:49,567
Switch the filter to all
pipelines, and it drops to 19%,

16
00:00:49,567 --> 00:00:55,532
because the Invisalign and reactivation
pipelines haven't closed anything yet this

17
00:00:55,532 --> 00:00:55,969
month.

18
00:00:56,819 --> 00:00:59,444
The funnel is where you find the leak.

19
00:00:59,444 --> 00:01:01,930
16 deals entered, and 4 reached Won.

20
00:01:01,930 --> 00:01:06,420
The percentages show how many made
it from one stage to the next.

21
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:09,183
Most stages keep three quarters or more.

22
00:01:09,183 --> 00:01:12,498
But only 57% of treatment
plans turn into a yes.

23
00:01:13,348 --> 00:01:15,796
That tells you exactly where to focus.

24
00:01:15,796 --> 00:01:18,051
Patients get a plan, then go quiet.

25
00:01:18,051 --> 00:01:22,948
A follow-up call two days after the
plan is sent, and a simple payment plan,

26
00:01:22,948 --> 00:01:24,430
could lift that number.

27
00:01:24,430 --> 00:01:27,201
You'll automate that
follow-up in Module 9.

28
00:01:28,051 --> 00:01:32,240
Stage distribution shows where your
open deals are sitting right now.

29
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:36,428
Three are still new enquiries, so
those people need contacting today.

30
00:01:36,428 --> 00:01:41,042
Remember, you can hide a stage from
these charts in the pipeline's settings.

31
00:01:41,896 --> 00:01:46,144
For a quick check without the
dashboard, the board itself is a report.

32
00:01:46,144 --> 00:01:51,182
Each column shows its count and value, and
the total for the whole pipeline sits at

33
00:01:51,182 --> 00:01:52,031
the top right.

34
00:01:52,031 --> 00:01:55,734
In list view, the same total
sits at the bottom of the table.

35
00:01:56,583 --> 00:01:58,820
Next, look at why deals are lost.

36
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:02,683
Open Advanced Filters, set
the status to lost, and apply.

37
00:02:02,683 --> 00:02:04,852
Each lost card shows its reason.

38
00:02:04,852 --> 00:02:09,665
If price keeps coming up, review your
pricing, or offer a payment plan.

39
00:02:10,517 --> 00:02:14,707
On the Pro plan, Reporting also
shows each team member's pipeline.

40
00:02:14,707 --> 00:02:19,215
Agent Reporting lists the deals each
person owns, how many they've won,

41
00:02:19,215 --> 00:02:20,993
and the value of those wins.

42
00:02:20,993 --> 00:02:22,771
Use it alongside the funnel.

43
00:02:22,771 --> 00:02:26,199
If one person's deals keep
stalling at the same stage,

44
00:02:26,199 --> 00:02:29,882
a little coaching on that step
can make a real difference.

45
00:02:30,732 --> 00:02:31,822
Here's a pro tip.

46
00:02:31,822 --> 00:02:34,772
Pick the one stage with
the lowest percentage,

47
00:02:34,772 --> 00:02:37,978
and change just one thing
about how you handle it.

48
00:02:37,978 --> 00:02:40,094
Then measure it again in a month.

49
00:02:40,094 --> 00:02:43,365
Small, focused fixes beat
big overhauls every time.

50
00:02:44,216 --> 00:02:45,833
That's Module 6 complete!

51
00:02:45,833 --> 00:02:50,359
You can now build a pipeline, work
it every day, and read its numbers.

52
00:02:50,359 --> 00:02:54,498
In Module 7, we'll start building
pages that bring new leads in,

53
00:02:54,498 --> 00:02:57,020
beginning with funnels versus websites.

54
00:02:57,020 --> 00:02:57,925
See you there!
